Rast wrote:
> You're right--the "@" character is currently the most heavily overloaded
> in nethack, since it contains nearly all of the huge variety of humans,
> and all of the elves.  And yet TDT feels that blobs, jellies, fungi, and
> puddings are so different from each other as to require four separate
> characters to represent them all...

Well, IMHO fungi should remain distinct, but combining blobs, jellies
and puddings seems sensible.

Let's see what we have here:

Sym  Colour  Monster
---  ------  -------
 b   green   acid blob
 b   white   quivering blob
 b   cyan    gelatinous cube
 j   blue    blue jelly
 j   green   spotted jelly
 j   brown   ochre jelly
 P   brown   brown pudding
 P   black   black pudding
 P   green   green slime

So we have three green things and two brown ones. We can make the ochre
jelly orange or red, and the spotted jelly could be any colour we like,
say magenta. Then we could make the acid below yellow, and bob's your
uncle. (I don't think the colours = hierarchy is really appropriate
here. These are the real colours of the blobs.)

This would leave 'P' and 'j' as symbols for other things. Any
suggestions what we could do with them?

